Package: lcdaGRASP
Type: Package
Title: GRASP and Reactive GRASP Algorithms for Joint Community and Leader Detection
Version: 0.3.1
Date: 2026-05-31
Authors@R: c(
    person("Andre", "Leite", email = "leite@de.ufpe.br", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Raydonal", "Ospina", role = "aut"),
    person("Geiza", "Silva", role = "aut"),
    person("Francisco Jucelino", "Matos Junior", role = "aut"),
    person("Luiz Satoru", "Ochi", role = "aut")
    )
Description: Implements the LCDA-GRASP and LCDA-GR (Reactive GRASP) algorithms
    for joint community-and-leader detection in complex networks, as proposed
    in Ospina et al. (2026). Performance-critical kernels (incremental
    modularity, community affinities, VNMI local search, power-iteration
    eigenvector centrality, HPI/Dice/Jaccard similarities) are implemented
    in C++ via Rcpp. An ensemble-consensus variant (LCDA-ECG) aggregates the
    GRASP pool into a consensus partition with overlapping communities and a
    per-node confidence map, and weighted graphs are supported through the
    modularity objective and local search. The package also includes the
    Node-Connection Entropy (NCE) leader score and its community-conditioned
    variant, statistical comparison utilities (Kruskal-Wallis + pairwise
    permutation). Reproducible
    analysis scripts (LFR robustness, pool sensitivity, Proposition 6 empirical
    convergence, and modularity-degeneracy analyses) are provided in the source
    repository.
